From 709628e4ba07f7f1551c4441b8088c93cae3d0c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:02:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: start over within this class when the chosen
 device cannot draw

When the graphics device that was chosen among several passes
InitDrm() but cannot be drawn with (gbm_create_device() fails), the
window system is started once more with the first device that has a
display. That second start was an unqualified call to
InitWindowSystem(), which is virtual: it ran the override of the class
that sets up EGL, and on its return the caller that was still running,
InitWindowSystemEGL(), set up EGL a second time. CEGLContextUtils
throws std::logic_error there, so Kodi would have ended where it was
meant to recover.

The call is now CWinSystemGbm::InitWindowSystem(). Before it, what was
read of the display of the device that is given up is dropped (display
information, EDID, whether it has Dolby Vision, whether the driver is
amdgpu): the first device may have another display, or one whose EDID
cannot be read, and those were only written over when there was one.

Found by the narrow re-read of the corrections. Read, not run: no
machine at hand has a device that fails that way.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
index 1930a79..e577669 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
@@ -233,7 +233,19 @@ bool CWinSystemGbm::InitWindowSystem()
                 __FUNCTION__);
       CDRMUtils::UseFirstDevice();
       m_DRM.reset();
-      return InitWindowSystem();
+      // nothing that was read of the display of that device is kept: the first device may have
+      // another display, or one whose EDID cannot be read
+      m_info.reset();
+      m_limitedInputPending = false;
+#ifdef HAVE_DVBRIDGE
+      m_displayEdid.clear();
+      m_dvInfo.reset();
+      m_dvDisplaySeen = false;
+      m_dvKernelAmdgpu = false;
+#endif
+      // This function and no override of it: the caller (InitWindowSystemEGL() of the class that
+      // was started) goes on with EGL when this returns, once.
+      return CWinSystemGbm::InitWindowSystem();
     }
 
     m_GBM.reset();
